[00:14.84] Silhouetted by the dawn
[00:17.02] The schoolboys shuffled and yawned
[00:21.44] Muffled underfoot by blankets of snow
[00:24.84] Observed by a solitary crow
[00:28.70] Traipsing across those wintry fields
[00:32.30] Me and my friends pretending to be ill
[00:36.54] Then wheeling away from school
[00:39.18] The humor turned cruel
[00:42.60] Platform soles of ice and mud
[01:10.74] Blazers of fur caked in blood
[01:15.10] In thicket dens on makeshift beds
[01:18.92] Quarts of cider spinning heads
[01:22.48] Faking intimacies with unobtainable girls
[01:25.72] Inventing futures in an uncertain world
[01:29.24] Like seeds on frozen soil the wind had blown
[01:33.18] Who can reap what cannot be sown?
[02:02.18] Others studied hard, stayed behind after class
[02:05.24] Convinced a better life might lie within grasp
[02:08.74] The relentless broadcasts in received pronunciation
[02:12.40] Consolidating this indoctrination
[02:15.72] But over-educated to the point of stupidity
[02:19.36] Many lost their spirit as well as their liberty
[02:23.28] Faced with a future, to which my kind is consigned
[02:26.50] I escaped with an empty head and an open mind
